  # CASES
  # == OP 18 UI CARD: count; screen width u16; height u16; density u32 in
  # 16 dot 16; then per ancestor nearest first: list container; root or
  # decor; width u16; height u16; answers the chain index or 254
  # A card is the first direct child of a list container other than the
  # label; else the last wide bounded ancestor two or more levels up:
  # ten widths reach seven screen widths; height reaches the larger of 80
  # and 80 times density; ten heights stay within eight screen heights
  # Numbers are little endian; sums carry and differences borrow one unit
  # at a time; kz holds one zero flag per byte level and kU the borrow out
  # %cell kn 128 %cell ksw 129 2 %cell ksh 131 2 %cell kd 133 4 %cell kp 137 4 %cell km 141 2
